eason to favor one?\n   - `Order of the Golden Cricket` activation is {W}. If I want to activate it multiple times? No, almost never beneficial (it just gains flying, multiple instances don't stack).\n   - I have 2 Plains, 1 Forest effectively (Thriving Heath counts as both).\n   - I have 2 White cards, 1 Green card in hand (plus Invoker).\n   - Played Plains seems slightly better to bluff multiple white spells? Or Forest to represent pump spells (usually green)?\n   - `Wildheart Invoker` is {8} to activate. Long way off.\n   - `Skyhunter Prowler` vs `Danitha`. Danitha is better (First Strike, Lifelink, Vigilance).\n   - Danitha costs `{2}{W}`.\n   - I should cast Danitha this turn.\n   - Wait, `Danitha` is in my hand. Why isn't she in `Choices`?\n   - `Choices (4): Dwynen's Elite [id=p3, cast, {1}{G}], Forest [id=p4, land], Plains [id=p23, land], Plains [id=p26, land]`\n   - Where is Danitha?\n   - Ah, I haven't played the land yet!\n   - Mana available: 2 lands untpped.\n   - I need to play a land first. The tool returns playable cards *based on current mana*.\n   - Once I play a land, Danitha will appear.\n\n   So, play land first.\n   Choice `p23` (Plains).\n\n   After land, I will have 3 mana.\n   Choices: `Danitha` (2W), `Prowler` (2W), `Elite` (1G).\n   Which is best?\n   - Danitha: 2/2 First Strike, Vigilance, Lifelink. Strong.\n   - Prowler: 1/3 Flying, Vigilance.\n   - Elite: 2/2 + possible 1/1 (if I have another Elf). I don't.\n   - Opponent has `Makeshift Battalion` (3/2).\n   - Danitha (2/2 First Strike) beats 3/2 in combat (strikes first, kills it, survives). Ideally she blocks or attacks safely.\n   - Prowler (1/3) blocks 3/2? No, takes 3 dmg, dies. 1 power deals 1 dmg.\n   - Prowler is an evasive threat (Flying). Opponent has `Makeshift Battalion`.\n   - Danitha is the board stabilizer and superior creature.\n   - Elite is just a 2/2.\n   - So Danitha is the pick.\n\n   Sequence:\n   1. Play Land (Plains).\n   2. Combat?\n      - My `Order of the Golden Cricket` (2/2) vs their empty board (Battalion is tapped? No, Battalion is 3/2 (sick). Sick = summoning sick, not tapped.\n      - Wait, Battalion was played last turn?\n      - Log: \"Turn 3 COMBAT... MstMed Sarge... bf=[Makeshift Battalion 3/2 (sick)...]\".\n      - If it is Turn 3 PRECOMBAT_MAIN for *Me* (actually Turn 4 for the game, if I went second? Or Turn 3 if I went first? The log says `Turn 3 PRECOMBAT_MAIN - Gem3P Hype`. Opponent attacked me in Turn 3 Combat. So this is Turn 3 Postcombat?\n      - Or is it Turn 4?\n      - \"Turn 3 COMBAT - Gem3P Hype\" was the previous log.\n      - No, `Turn 3 COMBAT` showed *my* board as defender. That was *Opponent's* turn (Turn 3).\n      - Now it's `Turn 3 PRECOMBAT_MAIN - Gem3P Hype`. Why \"Turn 3\" again?\n      - Game turns usually count up. Maybe MstMed Sarge was Active Player in Turn 3. Now it is Turn 3 for me?\n      - Ah, `Turn 3` in the log header might be \"Round 3\" or something.\n      - The `turns` count in Magic is usually \"Turn 1 (P1), Turn 1 (P2)\".\n      - The tool output says `Turn 3 PRECOMBAT_MAIN`.\n      - Regardless, it's my main phase.\n      - Opponent board: `Makeshift Battalion 3/2 (sick)`.\n      - If it was sick during their turn, it's still sick? No, sickness wears off at start of *controller's* turn.\n      - Wait. If it was sick on *their* turn, they just played it.\n      - Now it's *my* turn. It is technically not sick for blocking?\n      - Sickness only prevents attacking and {T} abilities. It *can* block.\n      - So `Makeshift Battalion` (3/2) is a blocker.\n      - My `Order of the Golden Cricket` (2/2).\n      - If I attack, 2/2 vs 3/2. They block, I die. They survive (3 toughness? No, 2 toughness).\n      - 3/2 vs 2/2 -> Trade.\n      - Do I want to trade my Cricket for their Battalion?\n      - Battalion grows if they get 3 attackers. It's a high priority threat.\n      - Trading is good.\n      - ALSO, I have {W} to give Flying.\n      - If I pay {W}, it's a 2/2 Flyer.\n      - Can 3/2 block Flying? No.\n      - So I can attack for 2 damage safely.\n      - BUT, paying {W} uses 1 mana.\n      - I have 3 lands. If I pay 1, I have 2 left.\n      - Can I cast Danitha (3 mana) then? No.\n      - Can I cast Elite (2 mana)? Yes.\n      - So:\n        Option A: Cast Danitha (3 mana). No attack mana. Attack? 2/2 ground into 3/2 ground. They block -> trade.\n        Option B: Pay Flying {W}. Attack for 2 in the air. Postcombat cast Dwynen's Elite (2/2).\n        Option C: Pay Flying {W}. Attack. Postcombat nothing (hold interaction? I have none).\n        Option D: Cast nothing, hold mana? Bad.\n\n   Comparison:\n   A: Board = Danitha (2/2 First Strike) + Cricket (dead? or bounced off?).\n      If I attack on ground, they likely block to kill my creature. Trade 2/2 for 3/2.\n      Result: Empty board vs Danitha. Strong position.\n      Danitha dominates the board.\n   B: Board = Elite (2/2) + Cricket (tapped). Life totals change (they take 2).\n      Next turn they untap with 3/2. They can attack?\n      If they attack with 3/2, I block with Elite (2/2). Trade.\n      Or takes damage.\n      Danitha is much better than Elite.\n      Danitha stops their attacks (First Strike) and gains life.\n\n   Conclusion: Cast Danitha.\n   Combat decision:\n   Should I attack with Cricket into Battalion?\n   If they block: Trade. Good for me (Battalion is better than Cricket).\n   If they don't block: 2 damage. Good.\n   So attacking is strictly good *if* I'm okay with trading.\n   With Danitha resolving post-combat (or pre-combat), I have a superior threat.\n   Wait, if I cast Danitha Pre-combat:\n   She has Vigilance? No, \"First strike, Vigilance, Lifelink\". Yes!\n   But she has summoning sickness, so she can't attack.\n   But she enters untapped.\n   If I cast her pre-combat, does it change their blocking math?\n   They see Danitha. They know I have a better blocker/attacker for next turn.\n   They might be more inclined to trade?\n   Or less?\n   If I attack with Cricket (2/2) into 3/2:\n   They block -> Trade.\n   They take -> I deal 2.\n   Is there any reason *not* to trade?\n   Cricket has the flying ability which is relevant late game.\n   Battalion has the Battalion ability which is scary if they go wide.\n   Battalion is the bigger threat. I should offer the trade.\n\n   So:\n   1. Play Plains.\n   2. Cast Danitha (Main 1).\n   3. Attack with Cricket (No flying activation).\n   \n   Why cast Danitha Main 1?\n   - In case she has Haste? No.\n   - To show strength?\n   - If I attack first and they have a removal spell (Instant), they might use it on Cricket? Unlikely.\n   - If I attack first, and offer trade, and they take it... board is empty. Then I drop Danitha. Strong.\n   - If I drop Danitha first, then attack... they see Danitha.\n   - Does seeing Danitha make them want to keep Battalion?\n     - Battalion vs Danitha: Danitha wins (First Strike).\n     - So Battalion is bad on defense against Danitha.\n     - They might as well trade Battalion for Cricket now while they can get value.\n     - So casting Danitha might *encourage* the block.\n     - Which is what I want (kill the Battalion).\n\n   So Plan: Play Plains -> Cast Danitha -> Combat (Attack with Cricket).\n\n   Let's execute the land drop first.\n\n",
