      "reasoning": "I missed the timing to cast Danitha?\nAh, because I played `Plains`, then it passed priority?\nUsually `pass_priority` tool stops at `stack_resolved`.\nPlaying a land doesn't use the stack, it just changes state.\nThen priority passes... to next *action*?\nWait, if I just played land, I should be in Main Phase still.\nWhy did it skip to Combat?\nMaybe I clicked `pass_priority` and it skipped?\nThe last tool call was `choose_action(choice=\"p23\")`.\nThe result says `next_action_message: Play spells and abilities`.\nThen I called `pass_priority`.\nThe result says `Turn 3 COMBAT`.\nSo `pass_priority` skipped `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` because I had no other actions?\nNO! I had Danitha playable. Why did it skip?\nMaybe I need to explicitly choose to act in Main Phase *before* passing priority?\nUsually `pass_priority` stops when I get priority.\nIn Main Phase, I have priority.\nDid the engine think I passed priority?\nWait, `pass_priority` documentation: \"Pass priority. Blocks until you have a pending action...\".\nIf I have playable cards, it *should* stop and let me play them.\nWhy did it skip to Combat?\nMaybe I played the land, then `pass_priority` was called with default arguments, and the server advanced?\nIf I had playable spells, `pass_priority` should have stopped.\nAh, looking at the previous turn `Turn 2 PRECOMBAT_MAIN`, I played `Thriving Heath` which enters tapped.\nDoes playing a land implicitly pass priority in some interfaces? No.\nMaybe the mana system is trippy?\nI have `Plains` (untapped), `Plains` (untapped), `Thriving Heath` (untapped).\nTotal 3 mana.\nDanitha costs {2}{W}.\nI have {W}{W}{G/W}. I can cast her.\nWhy didn't it stop?\nMaybe `combat_phase=\"declare_attackers\"` is where I am *now*.\nIt skipped Main 1?\nThis is bad.\nHowever, I can still cast Danitha in Postcombat Main.\nSo I should attack now.\n\nAttack with `Order of the Golden Cricket`.\nDo I pay {W} for Flying?\nIf I pay {W}, I have 2 mana left.\nThen in Post-Combat Main,