      "player": "Gem3P Hype",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "## Strategy Board Analysis:\nMy opponent is attacking with a 3/2 `Makeshift Battalion` into my `Danitha Capashen, Paragon` (2/2 with First Strike, Lifelink, Vigilance). Danitha was cast last turn? No, \"Turn 4 COMBAT - Gem3P Hype\".\nWait, if I cast her post-combat Turn 3, she was sick.\nNow it's Turn 4 (Opponent's turn).\nDanitha is no longer sick *on my turn*. But this is *opponent's* turn?\nAh, the label `sick` in the board description `bf=[Danitha Capashen, Paragon 2/2 (sick)...]` is confusing if it means \"summoning sick\".\nUsually summoning sickness wears off at the start of your upkeep.\nThis is Opponent's Turn 4. I cast Danitha in My Turn 3 Postcombat. So she has seen an upkeep (Opponent's upkeep? No, mine). Wait.\nTurn structure: Hype T3 -> Sarge T3 -> Hype T4? No.\nT3 Hype (me) -> T4 Sarge (opp).\nSo I just passed the turn.\nDanitha is summoning sick *until I start my next turn*.\nHowever, **summoning sickness does NOT prevent blocking**.\nOnly attacking and {T} abilities.\nDanitha is untapped (she has Vigilance but she wasn't declared as attacker because I cast her post-combat. Even if she was pre-combat, she doesn't tap to attack). She is untapped.\nShe is a 2/2 First Strike.\nAttacker is 3/2.\nFirst strike damage happens before normal damage.\nDanitha deals 2 damage to Battalion. Battalion dies.\nBattalion deals 0 damage to Danitha. Danitha lives.\n**This is a free kill.**\nUnless opponent has a combat trick.\nOpponent has `Mountain`, `Mountain`, `Plains` (untapped? No, look at `bf`).\n`bf=[Makeshift Battalion 3/2 (tapped), Mountain, Mountain, Plains, Thriving Heath (tapped)]`.\nAssuming standard output, unlisted state is usually untapped?\nOr `(tapped)` is explicit.\nSo `Mountain, Mountain, Plains` are untapped?\nThe previous turn they were tapped.\nThis is a new turn (Turn 4). They untap.\nAlso they played `Thriving Heath` (tapped).\nSo they have 3 mana open: `R`, `R`, `W`?\nCards in hand: 4.\nCombat tricks in this format (assuming generic card pool or similar set):\n- `Sure Strike` (+3/+0 First Strike)? If they give First Strike, 3/2 vs 2/2 trade.\n- `Built to Smash`?\n- `Kindled Fury`?\n- `Gideon's Reproach` (4 damage to attacker/blocker)?\n- `Shock` / `Lightning Bolt`?\nIf they have removal, they can kill Danitha.\nIf I don't block, I take 3 damage.\nDanitha is my best card. Losing her to a trick + trade is bad.\nLosing her to removal is inevitable if they have it (they can cast it whenever).\nIf I block, and they have a pump spell:\nThey spend a card to kill Danitha. I lose Danitha. They keep Battalion.\nIf I block, and they have *removal*:\nThey cast removal on Danitha. Danitha dies. Battalion lives ( and hits me? No, if removed before damage).\nWait, if they remove Danitha *before* damage, I take no damage from Battalion? No, if blocker is removed, attacker is still blocked, unless Trample (Battalion doesn't have Trample).\nSo blocking saves me 3 life even if she dies to removal.\nIf they have a Pump spell, she dies and I take no damage (unless Trample).\nIs it worth risking Danitha?\nDanitha (2/2 FS) vs 3/2.\nIf they have *nothing*, I kill their creature for free.\nWhy would they attack?\n1. They have a trick.\n2. They think I won't block because I fear a trick (bluff).\n3. They don't know First Strike rules? (Unlikely for competitive bot/player).\n4. They simply want to push damage or trade? (Trade isn't possible normally).\n\nGiven they are tapped out last turn but now have 3 mana open...\nIf they have `Gideon's Reproach` (WW or 1W?), they could kill her.\nBut blocking forces them to use it.\nIf I don't block, they keep the removal for later (e.g. for my flier).\nAND I take 3 damage.\nBlocking is generally correct unless Danitha is my *only* win condition and I can't risk her.\nI have `Skyhunter Prowler`, `Dwynen's Elite`, `Wildheart Invoker` (+ lands).\nI have other threats.\nBlocking saves 3 life and potentially trades 0 cards for 1 (if no trick) or 1 for 1 (if trick).\nA 1-for-1 trade where they use a trick (card) to kill my creature is fine.\nA free kill is amazing.\nThe only \"bad\" disaster is if they blow me out? e.g. `Coat with Venom` (Deathtouch)? Still 1-for-1.\nWait, First Strike kills Deathtouch before it hits back?\nYes! 2 dmg happens. 3/2 dies. Deathtouch creature deals 0 dmg.\nSo Deathtouch doesn't help them unless they survive the 2 damage. They have 2 toughness. They die.\nSo only *toughness boosting* tricks or *First Strike* tricks save them.\nOr removal.\nIf they have +2/+2 instant? 5/4 vs 2/2 FS.\nFirst Strike: 2 dmg to 5/4 (now 5/2).\nNormal Dmg: 5 dmg to 2/2 (dies).\nResult: Danitha dies. Battalion lives (with 2 damage marked).\nSo a pump spell wins the combat for them.\nIs that a risk worth taking?\nYes. Force the card out.\nAlso, maybe they are just bad/bluffing.\nThe upside (kill 3/2 for free) is huge.\nThe downside (losing Danitha to a pump spell) is acceptable compared to taking 3 damage freely and letting them keep their pump spell.\nI will block.\n\nTargeting: `blockers=\"p31:attacker_id\"`.\nAttacker ID?\n`Combat: Makeshift Battalion -> Gem3P Hype`.\nOpponent board: `Makeshift Battalion [id=p29]`. (Wait, ID is not shown in this summary?\nAh, standard pass_priority output often hides opponent IDs in the `bf` list text but usually reveals them in `combat` or `incoming_attackers`.\nThe prompt here doesn't show `incoming_attackers` explicitly.\nHowever, if I look at previous turns: \"Turn 3 COMBAT... Choices (1): Order of the Golden Cricket [id=p5]\".\nI need the attacker ID.\nOpponent Battlefield: `Makeshift Battalion 3/2 (tapped)`. No ID.\nI can call `get_game_state` again.\nOr I can guess `p29`?\nIt's risky to guess.\nBut I can observe previous turns if possible.\nIn `Turn 3 POSTCOMBAT`, opponent had `Makeshift Battalion 3/2 (sick)`.\nIn `Turn 3 COMBAT` (the one where I blocked Veteran), the opponent had `Makeshift Battalion [id=p29]`?\nI'll check the text from Turn 3 (my block turn).\nThe tool text was `Turn 3 COMBAT... bf=[Makeshift Battalion 3/2 (sick)...`.\nIt didn't show the ID.\nI called `get_game_state` in Turn 3!\nThe result was: `battlefield:[{id: \"p29\", name: \"Makeshift Battalion\"...}]`.\nYES! I have the ID from history. `p29`.\nIt's the same object (unless bounced and replayed, which is unlikely as it was sick last turn and tapped this turn).\nWait, if it was sick last turn, it's the same one (summoning sickness wears off).\nSo ID is `p29`.\n\nBlock `p31` (Danitha) on `p29` (Battalion).\n\nCall `choose_action(blockers=\"p31:p29\")`.\nAlso, chat: \"First Strike is a heck of a keyword, isn't it? Let's dance!\"\n\nWait, I should verify Danitha's ID.\nChoices: `Danitha Capashen, Paragon [id=p31]`. Confirmed.\n\nAction: Block.\n\n",
