      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "## Board State Review\nIt's my **Turn 4 Pre-combat Main Phase**.\n**Life:** Me 22, Opponent 18.\n**My Board:** `Danitha` (2/2 FS, Vig, Link - untapped), `Cricket` (2/2, can fly for {W} - untapped). `Plains`, `Plains`, `Thriving Heath` (tapped? No, lands untap). Total 3 lands.\n**Opponent Board:** `Siege Striker` (1/1 Double strike, sick), 5 lands (tapped).\n**My Hand:** `Craterhoof Behemoth` (8 mana - lol), `Dwynen's Elite` (2 mana), `Forest`, `Plains`, `Skyhunter Prowler` (3 mana), `Wildheart Invoker` (4 mana).\n**Resources:**\n- I have 3 lands in play.\n- I have a land drop: `Forest` or `Plains`. (Prefer `Forest` to enable `Wildheart Invoker` GG cost, or `Plains` if I need WWW). Currently have WWG available. Invoker needs 2GG. I have 1 G source (Heath). Playing Forest gives 2nd G source. Correct.\n- Playable Spells:\n    - `Skyhunter Prowler` {2}{W}: 1/3 Flying Vigilance. Good blocker/attacker.\n    - `Dwynen's Elite` {1}{G}: 2/2. No elf synergy trigger yet. Just a bear.\n    - `Wildheart Invoker` {2}{G}{G}: 4/3. Big body. 8 mana ability relevant late game.\n    - `Danitha` is already out.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. **Play Land:** `Forest`. Brings me to 4 lands: `Plains`, `Plains`, `Heath (G/W)`, `Forest (G)`.\n   Mana available: WWGG.\n2. **Post-Land Options:**\n   - Cast `Wildheart Invoker` (4 mana, 4/3). Biggest body on board. Beats `Siege Striker` (1/1 Double Strike becomes 2 damage first strike effectively, dies to 3 toughness? No. 1/1 Double Strike deals 1 first, 1 normal. 4/3 takes 1, kills 1/1. Easy win).\n   - Cast `Skyhunter Prowler` (3 mana). 1/3 flying. Evasive damage. Leaves 1 mana up.\n   - Cast `Dwynen's Elite` (2 mana). Leaves 2 mana up. Can hold up... nothing (no instants in hand).\n   - Attack with `Danitha` and `Cricket`.\n     - Danitha (2/2 First Strike): Opponent has `Siege Striker` (1/1 sick). Can block? Yes, sickness doesn't stop blocking.\n     - 1/1 Double Strike vs 2/2 First Strike:\n       Both have First Strike timing. They deal damage simultaneously in First Strike step.\n       Danitha deals 2 to Striker. Striker deals 1 to Danitha.\n       Striker dies. Danitha takes 1 damage (lives).\n       **So Danitha kills Striker for free.**\n     - Will they block? Probably not.\n     - So Danitha hits for 2 (Life -> 24).\n     - Cricket (2/2): If they block with Striker, Striker dies. Cricket takes 1 damage (lives).\n     - **Both attacks are profitable.**\n     - **I should attack with BOTH.**\n     - But wait, `Siege Striker` has \"Whenever this attacks, tap creatures... gets +1/+1\". It's sick now, so irrelevant. On their turn, if they tap out to pump it... scary. But I plan to kill it or race it.\n     - Actually, if I attack, they might not block.\n     - Then they untap and attack me with a huge Double Striker?\n     - `Siege Striker` gains +1/+1 for *each* creature tapped. They have 0 other creatures. So it can't get big yet unless they play more creatures (Haste?) or hold up blockers? No, tapping attacking/non-attacking creatures they control. They have no other creatures.\n     - So `Siege Striker` is just a 1/1 Double Strike for now.\n     - I should race.\n     - Danitha has Vigilance, so she attacks and blocks.\n     - Cricket doesn't have Vigilance.\n     - If I attack with Cricket, I can't block.\n     - 1/1 Double Strike hits me for 2 damage. I'm at 22. Fine.\n     - Race is in my favor.\n     - I will attack with both.\n     - Or maybe just Danitha if I want to be safe? No, 2 damage is 2 damage.\n\n3. **Sequencing:**\n   - Play `Forest` (Main 1).\n   - Cast `Wildheart Invoker` (Main 1 or 2)?\n     - If I cast Main 1, does it help? No Haste.\n     - If I attack first, they might trade? If they block Cricket with Striker -> Striker dies, Cricket lives. 1-for-0. Great.\n     - If they take 4 damage -> 14 life.\n     - Then cast Invoker 4/3.\n     - Invoker is a 4/3. Double Striker 1/1 can't attack into 4/3 effectively (1 dmg first strike -> 4/3 kills it).\n     - So Invoker is a great blocker too.\n     - Casting Main 2 is standard to hide info, but holding mana for tricks is useless (I have none).\n     - Showing the 4/3 might dissuade them? No, they have no actions.\n     - Just stick to Main 2 cast.\n\n   **Wait**, `Order of the Golden Cricket` Flying activation cost {W}.\n   If I want to fly over, I need {W}.\n   Opponent has only a ground creature (Siege Striker with Reach? No).\n   Striker can block ground.\n   As calculated, Striker dies if it blocks either of my 2/2s.\n   So Flying is unnecessary to push damage or save my creature.\n   Also I want to cast `Wildheart Invoker` (4 mana).\n   I have 4 lands total (3 + play one).\n   If I pay {W} for flying, I have 3 mana left.\n   Invoker costs 4. I cannot cast it.\n   So: **Do NOT pay for flying.**\n   Just attack on ground. If they block, they lose their creature. Win-win.\n\n   **Correct Line:**\n   1. Play `Forest`.\n   2. Enter Combat.\n   3. Attack with `Danitha` and `Cricket`.\n   4. (Declare attackers step) Decline flying payment.\n   5. (Combat ends) Main 2.\n   6. Cast `Wildheart Invoker`.\n   \n   This uses all mana efficiently, maximizes damage/board presence.\n\n   Let's start with Land.\n\n",
