    {
      "ts": "2026-03-02T18:58:57.689417-08:00",
      "seq": 100,
      "player": "Gem3P Hype",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I have 3 mana left and `Skyhunter Prowler` costs 3. I should cast it now.\n\nWhy now?\n- It has Vigilance, so it can block next turn even if I could attack with it (I can't, summoning sickness).\n- It increases my creature count for Craterhoof.\n- It taps out my mana, signaling I have no tricks, BUT\n- Opponent is tapped out? No, opponent has 5 lands untapped. He could have a board wipe.\n- If he wipes, I lose: Danitha, Cricket, Invoker, Elite, Elf Token, Prowler. That's a 6-for-1.\n- But if I don't play it, and he doesn't wipe, I missed a turn of development.\n- He's playing Red/White. Common wipes: `Planned Judgment`? `Settle the Wreckage`? `Cleansing Nova`? `Citywide Bust`?\n- Red/White usually relies on spot removal or \"damage to all creatures\" (e.g. `Deafening Clarion`).\n- Invoker (3 toughness) survives Clarion (2 dmg). Prowler (3 toughness) survives Clarion.\n- So playing Prowler is actually GOOD against 2-damage sweepers.\n- If he has a true Wrath (kill all), I'm screwed anyway with 5 creatures on board. Adding 1 doesn't change the \"I lose\" nature of a Wrath.\n- Better to maximize pressure. Prowler is a flyer, which puts him on a clock if the ground stalls.\n\nCast Prowler.\n\n",
      "toolCalls": [
        {
          "name": "choose_action",
          "arguments": "{\"choice\":\"p7\"}"
        }
      ],
