  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "MstMed Sarge declined to block Order of the Golden Cricket (2/2) with Makeshift Battalion (3/2, summoning sick). The Battalion would survive the block (taking 2 damage on 2 toughness... wait, 3/2 takes 2 damage and lives with 1 toughness) while killing the Cricket. Since the block was offered as legal, the Cricket doesn't have flying. By not blocking, Sarge takes 2 unnecessary damage and leaves the Cricket alive.",
      "actionTaken": "Declined to block, taking 2 damage and leaving Order of the Golden Cricket alive.",
      "betterLine": "Block Order of the Golden Cricket with Makeshift Battalion. The 3/2 survives combat against the 2/2 (taking 2 damage, living at 1 toughness) and kills the Cricket for free.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 71,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 20
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Thriving Heath's color choice timed out, likely defaulting to Blue or Black, neither of which is in MstMed Sarge's deck. They have Lightning Bolt in hand requiring red mana, and green cards (Dwynen's Elite, Wildheart Invoker) in their deck. Red would have been the optimal choice for immediate impact (casting Lightning Bolt), while Green would also have been reasonable for future cards.",
      "actionTaken": "Timed out on Thriving Heath color choice, defaulting to a likely useless color.",
      "betterLine": "Choose Red to help cast Lightning Bolt in hand and provide red mana flexibility alongside the two Mountains already in play.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 84,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 22
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Lightning Bolt cast was attempted to kill Danitha Capashen, Paragon during combat (which would have saved Makeshift Battalion from dying to first strike damage), but the mana plan was incorrectly specified causing the game engine to roll back the spell. Two untapped Mountains were available to pay {R}, but the mana plan referenced wrong permanent IDs. As a result, Makeshift Battalion died to Danitha's first strike damage while Danitha survived.",
      "actionTaken": "Attempted Lightning Bolt with an invalid mana plan (p1:1, p2:1), which was rolled back — effectively passing priority and losing the Battalion in combat.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Lightning Bolt targeting Danitha Capashen, Paragon with correct mana plan tapping a Mountain for {R}. This kills Danitha before first strike damage, saving the 3/2 Makeshift Battalion and removing opponent's lifelink/vigilance/first strike threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 92,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 27
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Failed to complete Lightning Bolt cast due to incorrect mana plan specification, despite having two untapped Mountains available to pay {R}. This resulted in Siege Striker dying to Danitha's first strike without accomplishing anything, while Danitha survived and the opponent gained 2 life from lifelink.",
      "actionTaken": "Attempted to cast Lightning Bolt with an invalid mana plan that was rolled back by the game engine, resulting in no action taken.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Lightning Bolt targeting Danitha Capashen with a correct mana plan (tapping a single Mountain for {R}). This would kill Danitha before first strike damage, saving Siege Striker and removing a key creature with first strike, vigilance, and lifelink.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 145,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 39
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "By passing priority with the Dwynen's Elite ETB trigger on the stack, Sarge missed the opportunity to Lightning Bolt Wildheart Invoker (3 damage kills the 4/3). With Wildheart Invoker dead, Dwynen's Elite's trigger would check 'if you control another Elf' on resolution and find no other Elves, so the 1/1 token would NOT be created. This would have been a 2-for-1: removing the biggest threat on the board AND preventing a token.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority, allowing Dwynen's Elite trigger to resolve and create a 1/1 Elf token while Wildheart Invoker remains on the battlefield.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Lightning Bolt targeting Wildheart Invoker in response to Dwynen's Elite's ETB trigger, killing the 4/3 and preventing the 1/1 token from being created.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 160,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 44
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 5 mana available and facing a board with a 4/3 Wildheart Invoker as the biggest threat, MstMed Sarge chose to cast Lightning Bolt (which can only kill a 2/2, removing 2 power) instead of Secure the Scene (which could exile the 4/3 Wildheart Invoker, removing 4 power and the dangerous {8} pump ability). At 14 life facing a wide board, removing the largest threat is more impactful.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Lightning Bolt (1 mana) to kill a 2/2 creature",
      "betterLine": "Cast Secure the Scene (5 mana) to exile Wildheart Invoker, removing the biggest threat and its pump ability, then save Lightning Bolt for a future turn or as removal for another creature",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 168,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 46
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lightning Bolt targeted Danitha Capashen, Paragon (2/2 with first strike, vigilance, lifelink) instead of Wildheart Invoker (4/3 with a game-ending pump ability). While Danitha's lifelink is relevant, the Wildheart Invoker represents the largest body on the board and has a devastating activated ability ({8}: +5/+5 and trample) that could end the game. MstMed Sarge is at 14 life with no creatures, so removing the biggest threat is more urgent.",
      "actionTaken": "Bolted Danitha Capashen, Paragon (2/2 first strike, vigilance, lifelink)",
      "betterLine": "Bolt the Wildheart Invoker (4/3) - it's the biggest body and has a game-ending activated ability. The opponent already has 5 other creatures; removing the largest threat with the most dangerous late-game potential is more impactful.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 169,
      "player": "MstMed Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 47
    }
  ],
